tee: optee: drop the dropped id argument from supp_pop_entry().

Adapted from
  https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/incr/patch-6.12.93-94.xz

6.12.93-94 reworked the supplicant request lifetime: request IDs live in
supp->idr and are assigned in optee_supp_thrd_req(), so supp_pop_entry() no
longer takes an `int *id`. The chain updated this file's call site but its
definition hunk found no context, leaving a three-argument definition with a
two-argument caller. One parameter goes.

--- a/drivers/tee/optee/supp.c
+++ b/drivers/tee/optee/supp.c
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@
 }
 
 static struct optee_supp_req  *supp_pop_entry(struct optee_supp *supp,
-					      int num_params, int *id)
+					      int num_params)
 {
 	struct optee_supp_req *req;
 
